      "incident_updates": [
        {
          "id": "fk89tlmlvg7j",
          "status": "scheduled",
          "body": "Datadog’s US1 status page is changing. Starting on October 29 2026, we’ll have a whole new look and experience based on Datadog’s own Status Pages product: https://docs.datadoghq.com/incident_response/status_pages/ \n\nThe new Datadog status page will be accessible via the same URL: https://status.datadoghq.com/. If you need to access the old version, you can find it at 1k6wzpspjf99.statuspage.io\n\nThe old status page will remain available, and Datadog will publish identical updates to both.\n\nNotifications will continue to be delivered to all existing subscribers.\n- Email notifications: On October 29, we will migrate all email subscriptions to the new status page. No action is required, and you will continue receiving email notifications as usual. Going forward, notifications will be sent from no-reply@dtdg.co.\n- Slack: Notifications via the old Slack integration will continue to be delivered until further notice. On October 29, we recommend upgrading to the Datadog Slack app to take advantage of the latest features (https://docs.datadoghq.com/incident_response/status_pages/#subscribe-in-slack)\n- RSS Feed: RSS feeds will continue normally. \n- SMS and Webhooks: Your existing subscriptions to SMS messages and webhooks will continue to be delivered. \n\nIf you typically view the Datadog status page via the web or supported subscription methods, no action is required. \n\nCustom integrations, workflows, and scripts that depend on the old status page url, structure, or API payloads may be affected by this transition. We recommend reviewing any custom integrations or code you have that pull data from Datadog’s status page. If you have custom integrations or code, you’ll need to take one of the following actions:\n\nChange the URL in your custom integration or code to point to the old version \nUpdate your custom integration or code to consume our new status page structure or payloads\n\nIf you have any questions, please respond to this email or reach out to our support team by visiting help.datadoghq.com.",
